{
 "description": "C.2 with two data constraints, prototyped in a script (description, discarded seeds).\n\nLogbook 127 found two freedoms the fit uses to discard what the perturbations test: every fit drives\nthe inhibitory wiring scale near zero, and the fitted PDF couplings came out inhibitory, where\nPDFR-1 couples to Galpha-s, which the layer's rule signs excitatory. Forcing PDF excitatory on the\nreadability answer turns pdfr-1's roaming change from +0.09 to -0.21, the real direction\n(`pdf_sign_check.json`). Two variants, each `screens.py`'s search on all six families at 64 animals\na candidate, with both guards, on 8 workers:\n\n- V1: the two chemical scales tied (the inhibitory scale is the excitatory one, so the connectome's\n  counts and signs set the balance) and PDF's two strengths held excitatory; from the imitation\n  answer (its scales already equal); population 48, sigma0 0.1, a cap of 300 generations.\n- V2: the inhibitory scale floored at 0.09 and PDF held excitatory; from the imitation's refinement\n  (mgl-1 at 0.61 of its wild type), its PDF strengths made positive; population 24, sigma0 0.05, a\n  cap of 200 generations.\n\nReadouts every 10 generations on the search's mean, on 200 shared animals (742,000,000 + i): every\nfamily graded, mgl-1 against its wild type, and the three Scheer mutants. Stop rules, timed after\nthe search's transient (V2's at two-thirds of V1's generations):\n\n1. the median score still above 1,000 at generation 60 (V2: 40);\n2. the readout D not at least 1 below its generation-0 readout by generation 120 (V2: 80);\n3. from generation 150 (V2: 100), three readouts in a row with mgl-1's early ratio at 0.9 or above\n   and pdfr-1's roaming change not negative.\n\nSeeds: V1 and V2 fit on 740 and 741 M (64\u00b7k + i), CMA 9483 and 9484. Run from the repository root:\n`prototypes.py V1` and `prototypes.py V2`, in parallel.\n",
